---
const items = [
  {
    q: 'Why iPhone first?',
    a: 'The habit we are designing for happens in a shop and in a cupboard, and a phone is what people have with them. Android is a documented follow-up, not an afterthought: the components are React Native and the design tokens already carry platform differences.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need smart shelves, a scanner or a hub?',
    a: 'No. The phone’s own camera reads barcodes, and typing remains the baseline path: everything stays usable without scanning anything. A scanned code is looked up for its product name and nothing else.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does my data live?',
    a: 'The device holds the working copy, so the app works on a train; signing in is optional and adds backup, second devices and sharing. The test server runs in the EU (Frankfurt). Where the released service runs will be stated here before there is anything to sign up for.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens if I delete my account?',
    a: 'It is deleted on the server, every phone is signed out, and this phone’s copy is erased. A household you shared with someone stays with them; one you used alone goes with your account.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does sharing work?',
    a: 'One person invites, the other enters a code. The code works once and expires after two days. Members can leave whenever they like; the owner can remove anyone.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will it cost money?',
    a: 'Not announced. What is decided is that the app will not be funded by showing you other people’s products: no ads, no data resale, no analytics on your shopping.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I try the beta?',
    a: 'There is no beta to join yet. When there is one, this page is where it will be announced.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why does this site have no cookies, fonts or analytics?',
    a: 'A page about a household inventory app should not itself inventory its visitors. This is static HTML and CSS — nothing third-party loads, and nothing is measured.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="shell stack">
    <header class="section__head section__head--center">
      <p class="t-overline">FAQ</p>
      <h2 class="t-headline" id="faq-title">Questions, answered</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="faq faq--narrow">
      {
        items.map((item) => (
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span class="t-label">{item.q}</span>
              <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">
                +
              </span>
            </summary>
            <p class="t-secondary measure">{item.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq--narrow {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .faq {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    border-block: var(--hm-border-hairline) solid var(--hm-border-subtle);
  }

  details {
    border-bottom: var(--hm-border-hairline) solid var(--hm-border-subtle);
  }

  details:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  summary {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--hm-space-card);
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: var(--hm-space-card) 0;
    list-style: none;
    min-block-size: var(--hm-touch-target);
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .chev {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    inline-size: 28px;
    block-size: 28px;
    border-radius: var(--hm-radius-pill);
    background: var(--hm-surface-secondary);
    color: var(--hm-text-secondary);
  }

  details[open] .chev {
    background: var(--hm-primary-subtle);
    color: var(--hm-on-primary-subtle);
  }

  details p {
    padding-bottom: var(--hm-space-card);
  }
</style>
